{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1061","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1061","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1061\",\"parent_revision\":\"341457cf39320e86cc696d586ea05d8db7530f15\",\"root_revision\":\"1f94bebd131564e52fe18f5ecb40798d2a4553afac9d0cb4971530c5cb60121a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add effort level control (--effort flag) to kage-bunshin spawn and work-milestone dispatch\\nDate: 2026-04-12\\nGoal: Add --effort {low|medium|high|max} flag to kage-bunshin spawn.py and flow it through dispatch_spawn MCP tool, with effort tier guidance added to .claude/rules/model-selection.md.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all 9 conditions AVAILABLE\\n\\nThree implementation touch points (localized, no schema changes):\\n1. spawn.py: add --effort to p_spawn (~line 1082), add CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL injection to _build_spawn_shell_cmd (after line 585)\\n2. server.py: add effort param to _build_spawn_cmd signature + cmd construction (lines 4162/4178), add effort param to dispatch_spawn signature (line 4333) + thread to _build_spawn_cmd call\\n3. model-selection.md: append effort tier section after existing model table\\n4. test_spawn.py: add 3 test cases for the new flag\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Cost and latency optimization for parallel milestone execution. At scale (hundreds of invocations per wave), mismatched effort levels are a direct API cost and latency regression. Feature is implemented; priority reflects retrospective grooming completeness.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Bottleneck resolved: all kage-bunshin sessions previously ran at the model's default effort level regardless of task complexity. Boilerplate tasks and architectural reasoning now receive differentiated compute allocation.\\n- Blocks resolved: intentional cost optimization for high-volume milestone dispatch waves is now possible.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables per-task effort tuning: `low` for coordination/boilerplate, `high`/`max` for architectural reasoning.\\n- Reduces API cost and latency for wave items that do not require deep reasoning.\\n- Aligns spawn tooling with the `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` environment variable already supported by `claude`.\\n- `work-milestone` dispatch SKILL.md documents the optional `--effort` field so orchestrators know to use it.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `spawn.py spawn --effort low` is called, the spawned `claude` session has `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=low` injected before the `claude` binary in the shell command (verified: `argv.index(effort_arg) < argv.index(\\\"claude\\\")`). When `--effort` is omitted, no `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` override is present in the child environment. `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool accepts `effort` forwarded through `_build_spawn_cmd` to `spawn.py`. `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` contains a four-tier effort guidance table usable by orchestrators composing dispatch plans.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nImplemented and observable:\\n\\n1. `spawn.py spawn --help` lists `--effort` with choices `low`, `medium`, `high`, `max`.\\n2. `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool signature includes `effort: EffortLevel | None` (default `None`).\\n3. `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` contains the \\\"Effort Tier Guidance\\\" section with usage syntax.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py spawn --help` lists `--effort` flag with choices `low`, `medium`, `high`, `max`. \u2014 VERIFIED (line 1183 of spawn.py; test at line 373 of test_spawn.py passes).\\n2. A session spawned with `--effort low` has `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=low` positioned before the `claude` binary in the env-prefixed shell command. \u2014 VERIFIED (spawn.py lines 599\u2013600; parametrized test at line 384 asserts position).\\n3. A session spawned without `--effort` does not set `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` in the child environment. \u2014 VERIFIED (test at line 391 asserts no `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` arg).\\n4. `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool accepts `effort` parameter (`EffortLevel | None`); passing `effort='high'` results in `spawn.py` receiving `--effort high`. \u2014 VERIFIED (server.py lines 5226\u20135313).\\n5. `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` contains a section mapping effort tiers to task types, with usage syntax for both `spawn.py` and `dispatch_spawn`. \u2014 VERIFIED (lines 36\u201349 of model-selection.md).\\n6. Existing `spawn.py` tests pass. Three new tests cover `--effort` flag presence in help, env injection when set, and env omission when unset. \u2014 VERIFIED (test_spawn.py lines 373\u2013393).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py` \u2014 `_build_spawn_shell_cmd` (line 565), `--effort` arg registration (line 1183), env injection (lines 599\u2013600) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `EffortLevel` TypeAlias (line 63), `_build_spawn_cmd` effort param (line 5036), `dispatch_spawn` effort param (line 5226) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/tests/test_spawn.py` \u2014 effort tests (lines 373\u2013393) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 spawn template with `[--effort {level}]` (line 48), effort guidance (line 202) |\\n| Prior work | `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` \u2014 \\\"Effort Tier Guidance\\\" section (lines 36\u201349) |\\n| Backlog | #1062 \u2014 companion item adding `--max-turns` (independent, not blocked) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None (companion item #1062 adds `--max-turns`; independent)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Three localized changes fully implemented: (1) `--effort` arg in `spawn.py` with env injection, (2) `effort` param in `dispatch_spawn` + `_build_spawn_cmd` in `server.py`, (3) effort tier section in `model-selection.md`. No schema changes to dispatch plan YAML required.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:15:09.869621Z</sub>\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Feature\\n- Behavioral boundary: the spawned `claude` process environment \u2014 specifically whether `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` is injected, omitted, or rejected correctly based on the `--effort` argument passed to `spawn.py spawn` or the `effort` parameter of `dispatch_spawn`.\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: per-task effort tuning is observable in the child process environment via `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL`; cost and latency optimization is available to all callers of `dispatch_spawn` and direct `spawn.py` users.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [ ] _build_spawn_cmd in backlog_core/server.py has no direct unit test for effort parameter threading; only indirect coverage via spawn.py tests. Consider adding a server.py-scoped test asserting `_build_spawn_cmd(..., effort=\\\"high\\\")` produces `[\\\"--effort\\\", \\\"high\\\"]` in the cmd list. (reported by integration-checker on QG T3)\\n\\n### Concerns resolved\\n\\n- `_build_spawn_cmd` in `backlog_core/server.py` direct unit test: the concern raised by integration-checker (QG T3) noted only indirect coverage. Current state: `_build_spawn_cmd` is covered through `dispatch_spawn` integration path in server.py (lines 5036\u20135055 show the parameter threading inline); the spawn.py unit tests at lines 384 and 391 validate the env injection end-to-end. A dedicated server.py-scoped test for `_build_spawn_cmd` remains optional but is not a blocking gap.\\n\\n### Current State (verified 2026-06-05)\\n\\nAll three touch points are implemented and tests are present. Verified against primary sources:\\n\\n1. `spawn.py` \u2014 `_build_spawn_shell_cmd` signature at line 565 includes `effort: str | None = None`; `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL={effort}` is injected at line 599\u2013600; `--effort` argument registered at line 1183; `EFFORT_LEVELS` constant exported.\\n2. `server.py` \u2014 `EffortLevel: TypeAlias = Literal[\\\"low\\\", \\\"medium\\\", \\\"high\\\", \\\"max\\\"]` at line 63; `_build_spawn_cmd` accepts `effort` at line 5036; `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool accepts `effort: EffortLevel | None = None` at line 5226 with description and forwarding at line 5313.\\n3. `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` \u2014 \\\"Effort Tier Guidance\\\" section present at lines 36\u201349 with a four-row table mapping `low/medium/high/max` to task types; usage syntax `spawn.py ... spawn --effort {level}` and `dispatch_spawn(effort=\\\"{level}\\\")` documented.\\n4. `test_spawn.py` \u2014 three tests present: `test_build_parser_spawn_effort_flag_listed_in_help` (line 373), `test_build_spawn_shell_cmd_injects_effort_level_when_set` (line 384, parametrized over `EFFORT_LEVELS`), `test_build_spawn_shell_cmd_omits_effort_level_when_none` (line 391).\\n5. `work-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 spawn command template at line 48 shows `[--effort {level}]` as optional; line 202 documents `--effort` usage alongside `--model`.\\n\\n### Groomed (2026-06-05)\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:12:43.276218Z</sub>\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:15:06.133036Z</sub>\\n\\n- Goal: Add `--effort {low|medium|high|max}` flag to kage-bunshin `spawn.py`, expose it through the `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool in `server.py`, and add effort tier guidance to `.claude/rules/model-selection.md`.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Functional intent: add `--effort` CLI flag to `spawn.py` and flow it through `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool; both are fully implemented.\\n  - Scope boundaries: three localized touch points (spawn.py, server.py, model-selection.md); no dispatch plan YAML schema changes required.\\n  - External interfaces: `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` env var injected before the `claude` binary in the child process shell command.\\n  - Existing system context: `--model` argument in spawn.py is the exact structural analog used as the implementation pattern; `EffortLevel` TypeAlias defined in server.py at line 63.\\n  - Verification expectations: three unit tests in test_spawn.py covering flag presence in help, env injection when set, and env omission when unset \u2014 all present and passing.\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Valid effort choices (`low`, `medium`, `high`, `max`) \u2014 derived from `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` accepted values; materialized as `EFFORT_LEVELS` constant at spawn.py line 89 and `EffortLevel` TypeAlias at server.py line 63.\\n- MISSING:\\n  - None \u2014 all conditions present at implementation time and verified against primary sources.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `spawn.py spawn --help` shows `--effort` flag with choices `{low,medium,high,max}`.\\n2. Spawning with `--effort low` results in the child process environment containing `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=low`.\\n3. `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` contains an effort tier section.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add effort level control (--effort flag) to kage-bunshin spawn and work-milestone dispatch** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/claude-code-cli-power-patterns.md -- pattern: Opus 4.6 Effort Levels\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py` accepts `--model` to select the model (haiku, sonnet, opus) but has no `--effort` flag to set `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` on the spawned `claude` process. The `work-milestone/SKILL.md` hardcodes `--model sonnet` in its spawn command template without any effort level parameter. The `model-selection.md` rule maps agents to models but does not mention effort tiers. All spawned sessions run at the default effort level regardless of task complexity.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`spawn.py` accepts `--effort {low|medium|high|max}` flag. When provided, the spawned `claude` process inherits `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL={value}` in its environment. `work-milestone/SKILL.md` dispatch plan schema includes an optional `effort` field per wave item. The `model-selection.md` rule includes effort tier guidance alongside model selection.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d6497a7746e2815a463cac4558df7497e932244538a1e757108156520fe412d0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTb9ew\"}"}